# MANDATORY: After-Hours AI Receptionist — master acceptance checklist

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-AFTER-HOURS-AI-RECEPTIONIST-MASTER-ACCEPTANCE-CHECKLIST.md`

## When this rule activates

Before **scoping**, **implementing**, or **declaring complete** any After-Hours AI Receptionist capability (wizard, Voice V3, GPT-Live, Astra, PSTN, booking, transfer, messages, after-hours rules).

## Hard requirements

1. **No scope invention** — New work maps to a section (1–27) in the master checklist. Do not open parallel “done” lists.
2. **✅ WORKING bar** — A checkbox is checked only when the **full real-world path** is proven (typically PSTN or production-equivalent E2E), not when UI saves, compiler maps, or a unit test passes alone.
3. **Wizard ≠ runtime** — Propagation/compiler tests are necessary but **insufficient** for marking checklist items complete.
4. **Update the doc** — When certifying a item, edit the master checklist in the same change set (check the box, add proof reference/date if useful).

## Authority order (after-hours)

1. This master acceptance checklist (functional completeness)
2. `docs/VOICE-V2-AFTER-HOURS-PRODUCT-CONTRACT.md` (architecture / one Amy)
3. Frozen pipelines where applicable (e.g. `docs/VOICE-V3-PSTN-BOOKING-PIPELINE-FROZEN.md`)
4. Implementation code
